WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.190
Avengers; Infinity War ended with the biggest
downer since The Empire Strikes Back, so it’s

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:08.809
no wonder that everyone’s trying to figure
out what’s going to happen when Thanos returns

00:00:08.809 --> 00:00:11.020
to the screen in 2019.

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:14.400
From clues we’ve picked up from the comics
to hints that we’ve already seen, here are

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.570
our predictions for the possible outcomes
of Avengers 4.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:22.390
Spoiler warning: we’re going to be talking
a lot about the end of Infinity War.

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:23.970
The New Black Panther

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:28.100
The most shocking part of Infinity War came
when Thanos snapped his fingers and killed

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:33.300
half the universe, and it only got more surprising
when it turned out that half included heroes

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.750
like Spider-Man, Bucky, Doctor Strange, and
the Black Panther.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:42.450
Since there are about 1.3 billion reasons
and counting to keep that last guy around,

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:46.410
we’re guessing that most of those deaths
are probably going to be undone by the end

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:47.510
of Avengers 4.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:51.380
"As you can see, I am not dead."

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:55.730
Even if it’s just for now, though, T’Challa’s
death leads to the most obvious idea for the

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:59.190
next one: Shuri becoming the new Black Panther.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:03.380
With the heart-shaped herbs gone at the end
of Black Panther, Shuri would be able to use

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:06.240
her expertise with technology to step into
the role.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:10.439
We've even seen her in action, fighting with
panther-shaped energy gauntlets.

00:01:10.439 --> 00:01:12.229
All she needs is the costume.

00:01:12.229 --> 00:01:16.909
The other strong possibility would be that
Nakia takes over instead, but Shuri's the

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:21.450
one who becomes Black Panther in the comics
when T’Challa is incapacitated.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:25.049
With Marvel Studios' track record of using
elements from stories like Winter Soldier

00:01:25.049 --> 00:01:29.990
and Infinity Gauntlet as road maps, that seems
like one they'd want to stick with.

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:31.469
King of the Dead

00:01:31.469 --> 00:01:35.259
If Shuri does become the Black Panther, that
leaves us with the question of what could

00:01:35.259 --> 00:01:36.359
happen with T’Challa.

00:01:36.359 --> 00:01:39.979
We’re pretty sure he’s going to come back
to life somehow, but something in the comics

00:01:39.979 --> 00:01:44.240
gives another possibility: he might just become
the King of the Dead.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:48.799
In the comics, T’Challa found himself conflicted
after Shuri took over as the leader of Wakanda.

00:01:48.799 --> 00:01:53.740
He wanted to be Black Panther again, but he
doesn't want to interfere with Shuri’s reign.

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:57.680
Obviously, he solves this problem by going
to the secret necropolis under the Golden

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.450
City so that he can talk to Bast, the cat
goddess.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:02.719
You know, pretty standard cat stuff.

00:02:02.719 --> 00:02:07.429
To give him a new purpose, she made him King
of the Dead, with all the strength and wisdom

00:02:07.429 --> 00:02:09.640
of every Black Panther before him.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:13.880
Who better to lead a team of superheroes back
to the land of the living than him?

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:15.930
Asgard Reborn

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:19.040
Infinity War’s shocks aren’t limited to
the end of the movie.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:24.150
Right at the beginning, we find out that Thanos
and the Black Order killed all of the Asgardian

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:27.760
refugees that Thor worked so hard to save
in Ragnarok.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:30.099
That might not be the end of Asgard, though.

00:02:30.099 --> 00:02:34.440
In the comics, Ragnarok isn't the end of the
world, it's the end of a cycle.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:39.480
As gods, Thor and the other Asgardians are
creatures of mythology — they live, die,

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:43.520
and are reborn into new forms, eternally bound
by their nature.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:47.760
If we're following that logic, then the next
major quest for a Thor who's more powerful

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:52.160
than ever could be the rebuilding of Asgard
by tracking down the reborn souls of the other

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:55.660
gods — including an all-new, all-different
Loki.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:57.850
The return of Korg, Miek, and Valkyrie

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:04.280
They couldn’t really kill the three best
new movie characters of 2017 offscreen between

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:05.579
movies, could they?

00:03:05.579 --> 00:03:10.030
Until proven otherwise, let’s just assume
that Korg, Miek, and Valkyrie weren't on the

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:11.960
refugee ship for some reason.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:15.720
Maybe they were out scouting for groceries,
or fighting the Skrulls.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.400
Anything to get them back for next time.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:22.081
Seriously: If Happy Hogan can be in like six
of these movies, then Valkyrie needs to be

00:03:22.081 --> 00:03:23.950
in at least ten.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:25.380
Tony Stark, R.I.P.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:30.050
A lot of moviegoers predicted that we’d
be bidding a fond farewell Robert Downey Jr.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:31.550
in Infinity War.

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:35.240
That didn’t happen this time, but it may
have been set up for Avengers 4.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:39.910
Doctor Strange traded Thanos the Time Stone
in exchange for sparing Tony Stark's life.

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:44.580
That's surprising, first because Strange swore
an oath to protect it, and second because

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:49.780
he did it knowing that if Thanos got the stones,
he was going to kill half the galaxy anyway.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:54.490
Even if Strange and Stark were BFFs and not
just dudes who didn't actually seem to like

00:03:54.490 --> 00:04:00.410
each other, there's no way anyone should trade
Iron Man's life for uncountable trillions.

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:01.570
Unless…

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:05.780
Shortly before that scene is the one where
Strange uses the time stone to take a peek

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:11.030
at 14 million alternate outcomes, and says
that the good guys only win in one.

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:15.180
Given the bargain he makes, you have to assume
that the one reality where Thanos is defeated

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:20.049
has to be one where Tony Stark lives long
enough to do something to turn the tide.

00:04:20.049 --> 00:04:25.110
We’re betting it’s a heroic sacrifice
that's been building for 11 years.

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:26.830
The All-New Iron Man

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:30.940
Tony Stark might be on the way out, but Iron
Man could stick around.

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:34.020
It's just going to be Jim Rhodes under the
helmet instead.

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:37.520
Like Shuri, this one follows the precedent
set in the comics.

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:41.970
Before he was War Machine, Rhodey was Iron
Man from 1983 to 1985.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:45.550
It also seems like a logical continuation
of the story.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:50.249
He's the only one besides Tony to fight in
the Iron Man armor, and the big airport battle

00:04:50.249 --> 00:04:54.039
in Civil War left him injured, needing Stark's
tech to walk.

00:04:54.039 --> 00:04:57.780
That puts him in a very similar position to
the way Tony was back in his early comics

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:00.860
appearances, when he needed his armor to keep
his heart beating.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:06.960
If Rhodey does take over, that provides proof-of-concept
for the idea that the MCU can continue after

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:11.129
the departure of big-name actors, something
that was already done on a small scale when

00:05:11.129 --> 00:05:14.490
Don Cheadle took over the role of Rhodey from
Terrence Howard.

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:16.669
"Next time, baby."

00:05:16.669 --> 00:05:18.710
Keep waiting for Adam Warlock

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:22.770
Adam Warlock is a huge part of the original
Infinity Gauntlet story.

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:26.659
While his role for the most part is limited
to standing around in space watching the big

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:32.550
battle go down, he actually winds up in possession
of the Gauntlet itself at the end.

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:36.229
Between that and his imminent arrival being
teased in the post-credits scene of Guardians

00:05:36.229 --> 00:05:40.919
of the Galaxy Vol. 2, it might have been surprising
that he didn’t make an appearance in Infinity

00:05:40.919 --> 00:05:41.919
War.

00:05:41.919 --> 00:05:46.749
He’s even the focal point of the comic book
crossover that gave the movie its name.

00:05:46.749 --> 00:05:50.189
If you’re thinking they might have saved
him for the sequel, though, it doesn’t seem

00:05:50.189 --> 00:05:51.189
likely.

00:05:51.189 --> 00:05:54.680
One of the few movies to have actually been
announced for the next phase of Marvel movies

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:57.610
was Guardians of the Galaxy Volume 3.

00:05:57.610 --> 00:06:02.139
With Adam being set up as Ayesha’s genetically
engineered instrument of revenge, it’s way

00:06:02.139 --> 00:06:04.580
more likely that he’ll show up there.

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:09.319
That leaves the role open for a space-faring
hero who can explain galactic conflicts, and

00:06:09.319 --> 00:06:12.830
it seems pretty obvious that it’s going
to go to Captain Marvel, who was summoned

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:16.790
at the end of Infinity War by Nick Fury’s
cosmic beeper.

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:21.059
That makes sense structurally, since Captain
Marvel and Ant-Man and the Wasp are the only

00:06:21.059 --> 00:06:25.020
MCU movies coming out between Infinity War
and Avengers 4.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:28.699
As much as we like Scott Lang, he’s not
the guy who’s going to be getting everyone

00:06:28.699 --> 00:06:31.629
up to speed on the Kree/Skrull War.

00:06:31.629 --> 00:06:35.749
Carol Danvers, on the other hand, has experience
battling against and wielding exactly the

00:06:35.749 --> 00:06:40.370
kind of cosmic power that the heroes are going
to need to beat Thanos once and for all.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:44.069
That leaves the Guardians free to fly back
into their own movie, and the only question

00:06:44.069 --> 00:06:49.110
left is whether they’ll fight Adam Warlock
or the Magus, who is Adam Warlock’s evil

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:51.389
self from an alternate future.

00:06:51.389 --> 00:06:53.650
Comic books can be pretty complicated.

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:54.860
Capwolf at last

00:06:54.860 --> 00:07:00.090
We’ll admit that this one’s pretty unlikely,
but if Infinity War has proven anything, it's

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:03.560
that the Marvel movies can do anything and
make a billion dollars.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:07.930
They've spent ten full years and 19 movies
getting to that point, but they just put out

00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:12.729
a movie about a giant purple man trying to
get his hands on magic space rocks, featuring

00:07:12.729 --> 00:07:17.849
characters like Proxima Midnight and the Collector,
and a major plot point was that a space dwarf

00:07:17.849 --> 00:07:20.139
made a magic hammer out of a talking tree.

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:23.259
We’re not complaining, but you have to admit
that stuff’s pretty weird.

00:07:23.259 --> 00:07:27.210
Clearly, there’s nothing stopping them from
doing a movie where Captain America becomes

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:32.689
a super-powered werewolf and delivers an inspirational
speech to a bunch of other werewolves.

00:07:32.689 --> 00:07:35.889
It might even make sense from a movie-making
standpoint.

00:07:35.889 --> 00:07:40.159
If Chris Evans really does want to scale back
his acting work and devote his time to remodeling

00:07:40.159 --> 00:07:44.720
his house, then why not replace him with a
CGI wolfman with an indestructible shield?

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:49.159
It would definitely be a weird direction to
lift from the comics, but they already did

00:07:49.159 --> 00:07:51.919
the part where Thanos starts turning people
into cubes.

00:07:51.919 --> 00:07:55.030
There’s no way a wolf is any weirder than
that.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:56.080
Thanks for watching!

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:58.649
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:58.649 --> 00:08:00.669
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

